me": "Goeller M", "lastName": "Goeller", "firstName": "Markus", "initials": "M"}, {"fullName": "Betancur J", "lastName": "Betancur", "firstName": "Julian", "initials": "J"}, {"fullName": "Cadet S", "lastName": "Cadet", "firstName": "Sebastien", "initials": "S"}, {"fullName": "Doris M", "lastName": "Doris", "firstName": "Mhairi", "initials": "M"}, {"fullName": "Chen X", "lastName": "Chen", "firstName": "Xi", "initials": "X", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-3855-2591"}}, {"fullName": "Berman DS", "lastName": "Berman", "firstName": "Daniel S", "initials": "DS"}, {"fullName": "Slomka PJ", "lastName": "Slomka", "firstName": "Piotr J", "initials": "PJ", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-6110-938X"}}, {"fullName": "Tamarappoo BK", "lastName": "Tamarappoo", "firstName": "Balaji K", "initials": "BK"}, {"fullName": "Dey D", "lastName": "Dey", "firstName": "Damini", "initials": "D", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-2236-6970"}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-6110-938X"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-2236-6970"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-3855-2591"}]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "8", "volume": "37", "journalIssueId": 2712498, "dateOfPublication": "2018 Aug", "monthOfPublication": 8, "yearOfPublication": 2018, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "IEEE Trans Med Imaging", "title": "IEEE transactions on medical imaging", "essn": "1558-254X", "issn": "0278-0062", "nlmid": "8310780", "isoabbreviation": "IEEE Trans Med Imaging"}, "printPublicationDate": "2018-08-01"}, "pubYear": "2018", "pageInfo": "1835-1846", "abstractText": "Epicardial adipose tissue (EAT) is a visceral fat deposit related to coronary artery disease. Fully automated quantification of EAT volume in clinical routine could be a timesaving and reliable tool for cardiovascular risk assessment. We propose a new fully automated deep learning framework for EAT and thoracic adipose tissue (TAT) quantification from non-contrast coronary artery calcium computed tomography (CT) scans. The first multi-task convolutional neural network (ConvNet) is used to determine heart limits and perform segmentation of heart and adipose tissues. The second ConvNet, combined with a statistical shape model, allows for pericardium detection. EAT and TAT segmentations are then obtained from outputs of both ConvNets. We evaluate the performance of the method on CT data sets from 250 asymptomatic individuals. Strong agreement between automatic and expert manual quantification is obtained for both EAT and TAT with median Dice score coefficients of 0.823 (inter-quartile range (IQR): 0.779-0.860) and 0.905 (IQR: 0.862-0.928), respectively; with excellent correlations of 0.924 and 0.945 for EAT and TAT volumes. Computations are performed in <6 s on a standard personal computer for one CT scan. Therefore, the proposed method represents a tool for rapid fully automated quantification of adipose tissue and may improve cardiovascular risk stratification in patients referred for routine CT calcium scans.", "publicationStatus": "ppublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Print-Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["research-article", "Journal Article", "Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural"]}, "grantsList": {"grant": [{"agency": "NHLBI NIH HHS", "acronym": "HL", "grantId": "R01 HL133616", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute", "grantId": "1R01HL133616", "orderIn": 0}]}, "meshHeadingList": {"meshHeading": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Thorax", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "DG", "qualifierName": "diagnostic imaging"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Pericardium", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "DG", "qualifierName": "diagnostic imaging"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Adipose Tissue", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN"